    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **65 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `AuditOwnerCreated.java` (the `audit` step of the `POST /api/owners` pipeline).\n\nAlongside the existing human-readable audit line, it now emits a second line on the same `AUDIT` logger \u2014 an immutable JSON event:\n\n```json\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- **`seq`** is backed by a `static AtomicLong` incremented per create, so it is monotonically increasing across all creates in the instance.\n- **`membershipLevel`** reuses the household-capped value already computed for the audit line, so the event and the line stay consistent with the response.\n- **Primary identifier via `primaryIdentifier(Owner)`** \u2014 this helper returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. The spec's future requirement (customerCode unified into `memberId`) is satisfied by changing that one method to return the memberId; the event automatically carries the new identifier with no other change. This intent is documented in the method's Javadoc.\n- **`jsonString(...)`** escapes the identifier defensively so the emitted line is always valid JSON, and the `{}` SLF4J placeholders are distinct from the literal JSON braces (no `{}` collisions).\n\nThe new `Cp53Tests` (audit-event) passes, and the previously passing `Cp21Tests` (audit line has region-hash code) and `Cp43Tests` (audit line includes level/number) remain green since the original line was preserved unchanged.",
